WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.940
Rapping up the week on Tesla's short time, daily, episode 480. Patrick here in Vancouver,

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:14.320
it's May 22nd, 2026. Here's what's wrapping up the week in Tesla land. Tesla's first model

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:20.220
Y price increase in two years test weather buyers will absorb higher costs amid softening demand.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:27.880
Tesla quietly increased prices on three model Y trims in the United States. The move marks the first

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:34.080
upward adjustment in nearly two years and affects the entry level rear wheel drive and long range

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:40.360
variance. Buyers now face higher transaction prices at a moment when inventory levels have grown

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:47.480
and incentives remain limited. The change comes as Tesla balances production capacity with shifting

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.380
order patterns across its highest volume model. Watch for whether the adjustment slows weekly

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:58.860
delivery rates or prompts more leasing activity in the coming quarter. After looking at

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:04.140
pricing pressure on the highest volume model, let's shift to how Tesla is changing the way

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:11.260
customers pay for its most advanced software. New buyers in Europe can now access full self-driving

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:17.340
only through a monthly subscription. Just two countries have so far approved supervised FSD

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:23.820
operation, limiting immediate rollout scale. The policy shift removes the previous outright

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:29.720
purchase path that existed in other markets. Tesla is aligning payment structure with regulatory

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:36.140
approval timelines rather than hardware capability alone. The next data point will be subscription

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.460
uptake once additional countries clear the software. While Europe tests the subscription approach,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:49.560
Tesla has just activated supervised FSD in another major market after years of delay. Tesla activated

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:56.080
full self-driving supervised for eligible vehicles in China. The software arrives years after initial

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:02.200
testing began and after several local competitors launched similar features. Early access is

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:08.180
limited to cars with compatible hardware and updated maps. Tesla is using the launch to gather

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:14.240
localized driving data for further refinement. Uptake numbers in the first month will reveal whether

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:22.000
owners value the added capability enough to subscribe. With FSD expanding in China, Tesla is also

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.420
scaling the team that will support it. Tesla is actively recruiting engineers and software

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.720
specialists to support its China autonomy efforts. The push follows regulatory approval for supervised

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:39.660
full self-driving in the country. New hires will focus on local mapping, regulatory compliance,

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:46.000
and integration with domestic data centers. The expansion signals Tesla's intent to close the gap

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.640
with Chinese rivals already offering comparable features. Hiring volume and roll seniority will

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.520
indicate how quickly the team can scale. While Tesla builds capability in China, it's also managing

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:05.240
service issues closer to home with the cyber truck. Tesla is using remote diagnostics to flag power

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:11.640
conversion system failures on cyber trucks. Effected owners receive free supercharging credits while parts

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:17.540
are sourced for repair. The program covers vehicles still under warranty and aims to reduce downtime

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:23.620
during the parts wait. Early data shows the failures cluster around specific mileage bands.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.720
Continued monitoring will determine whether the issue requires a broader service campaign.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:34.900
From vehicle service challenges, let's look at how Tesla is handling a narrow but formal recall on

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:40.860
the Model Y. The recall targets vehicles that may lack a required certification sticker on the

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:46.880
driver side door. Tesla identified the issue through internal checks and will remedy affected units

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.600
at service centers. The scope remains narrow compared with earlier camera-related recalls

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:58.660
but still requires owner notification and scheduling. Regulators treat the missing label as a

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:04.340
compliance matter rather than a safety defect. Owners should expect letters directing them to

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:10.460
schedule the free fix. On the regulatory side, a competitor is preparing its own large scale

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:18.440
response to Tesla's autonomy push. Stellantis detailed plans for new low-cost LFP battery platforms and

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:23.920
in-house autonomy hardware. The investment targets a direct response to Tesla's supervised,

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:30.680
full-self driving stack. The company is pairing cheaper cells with high-performance chips to enable

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:38.100
competitive driver assistance features. Production timelines stretch into 2027 and 2028 for the first

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:44.180
vehicles. Competitive pressure will depend on how quickly Stellantis can validate its system on

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:50.460
public roads. Taking a step back from today's headlines, the decision to move full-self driving in

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:56.520
Europe to a subscription-only model challenges the assumption that one time hardware purchases best

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:02.780
match customer willingness to pay. Subscription pricing ties revenue directly to ongoing software

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:09.180
performance and regulatory approval in each country. In markets where only two nations have cleared

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:15.280
supervised operations so far, the model lets Tesla capture value without locking buyers into a

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:22.160
large upfront sum that may not deliver immediate unsupervised capability. Data from early subscription

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.860
uptake will reveal whether owners treat the feature as a recurring utility or a discretionary add-on.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:33.580
If adoption stays strong, the approach could reshape how Tesla finances autonomy development

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:40.160
across regions with staggered regulatory timelines. It also reduces the risk of stranded capital

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:46.460
if future software versions require additional hardware upgrades. The shift tests whether recurring

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:51.860
revenue can stabilize cash flow even as vehicle margins face pressure from price competition.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:58.260
Keep an eye on subscription uptake numbers in Europe and hiring progress for the China autonomy team

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:05.580
as both stories develop next week. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at 417

